{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but UART RX got 0xff (idle) vs expected 0xa5. TX bit-period test `send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)` in excerpt divides the divider by 16, so TX shifts ~16x too fast and returns to idle before RX samples. RX therefore samples all-ones.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,10 +125,10 @@
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no uart data mismatch trap, loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

